description:
three edits, one test, one file.

In repos/development-vessel/test/resolvers/orphaned-capability-scan.test.ts, the test "emits an orphaned_capability gap for a live, never-invoked outward capability" asserts on emits[0]. The harness wireSubstrate captures EVERY POST to /v2/impulses/resolve, and the resolver reads substrateGap twice before it writes, so emits[0] is a READ. The assertion fails: Expected "substrateGap_write", Received "substrateGap".

Do not change src/resolvers/orphaned-capability-scan.ts. The resolver is correct — body.gaps_emitted is 1 in this same test and that assertion already passes, so exactly one write occurs. The test measures the wrong thing.

Three edits. Each anchor is unique in the file. Use them verbatim.

EDIT 1 — replace this exact line:

    expect(emits[0].impulse.pointer.type).toBe("substrateGap_write");

with these two lines:

    const _w = emits.filter((e: any) => e.impulse.pointer.type === "substrateGap_write");
    expect(_w.length).toBe(1);

EDIT 2 — replace this exact line:

    expect(emits[0].impulse.pointer.gap.category).toBe("orphaned_capability");

with:

    expect(_w[0].impulse.pointer.gap.category).toBe("orphaned_capability");

EDIT 3 — replace this exact line:

    expect(emits[0].impulse.pointer.gap.id).toBe("orphaned-capability-problem_detection");

with:

    expect(_w[0].impulse.pointer.gap.id).toBe("orphaned-capability-problem_detection");

Change nothing else. Leave wireSubstrate, TEMPLATES, the imports, and every other test in the file exactly as they are. The other four failing tests in this file are a separate gap and must not be touched here.

ORACLE — verified reachable, not assumed: applying exactly these three edits to a scratch copy takes the file from 1 pass / 5 fail to 2 pass / 4 fail. The four remaining failures belong to the separate gap and are expected to persist.

The file must typecheck. This vessel carries a standing baseline of pre-existing failures elsewhere — judge on newly-failing tests, not absolute counts.

